The problem is that `PricingRules.standardDiscountFor` runs one SOQL query per call. Calling it once per line in a 200-line quote blows the 100-query limit. The pricing logic must stay in `PricingRules`, so I won't change it or duplicate its rules. Instead, the handler caches the resolved discount per product within the transaction, so `PricingRules.standardDiscountFor` is invoked once per distinct product while still being the single source of the rule. Lines that already have a `Discount` (including `0`) are left untouched.

